# MCU firmware (`src/mcu`)

PlatformIO board `esp32dev`. Entry: `src/mcu/src/main.cpp`.

## Hardware flow

Keypad ID → `#` → `LOOKUP` → enroll (SET) or verify (GET) knocks → servo door on success.

## Enroll (SET)

1. Capture primary pattern.
2. Capture confirm pattern.
3. Local `patternsConfirmMatch` (same rhythm idea as host).
4. On match only: `SET:<id>:<gaps>`. On mismatch: abort, do not upload.

## LCD

- Short uppercase military tone (≤16 chars/line): `STANDBY`, `ENROLL COMPLETE`, `ACCESS DENIED`, etc.
- Avoid casual phrasing (“Ready”, “Oops”).

## Ops

- Close serial monitor before `pio run -t upload` (COM port lock on Windows).
- WiFi SSID/password and `SERVER_HOST` live as constants in `main.cpp`.
- Keep knock tuning constants (`KNOCK_*`) centralized; timer starts after first accepted knock.
- Tap input: two wires GPIO32↔GND. 100ms merge window; 3s idle ends pattern. Gaps = ms between taps.
- Flow helpers: `runEnroll` / `runVerify` / `captureTaps` — keep military LCD ≤16 chars.
